# Citation metadata for this repository (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# GitHub renders this as "Cite this repository". Version/date track the last public
# status update; bump at v1.0.0 (EP-163). This cites the *software*; anyone using
# the warehouse must also cite the MIMIC-IV datasets and PhysioNet — see
# "source material/README.md" § Citations — and mimic-code (NOTICE).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the MIMIC-IV datasets and PhysioNet as listed in source material/README.md."
type: software
title: "mimicwarehouse: a local MIMIC-IV data lab (DuckDB + Parquet warehouse, Python backend, Streamlit Lab)"
abstract: >-
  A local, single-machine data lab over MIMIC-IV 3.1, MIMIC-IV-ED 2.2 and MIMIC-IV-Note 2.2:
  a DuckDB + Parquet warehouse with a Python backend and a Streamlit "Lab" app for exploratory
  analysis and protocol-frozen inquiry over retrospective EHR data, with end-to-end provenance
  and small-cell disclosure discipline. Work in progress; the PhysioNet-licensed data are not
  part of the repository.
authors:
  - family-names: Farrington
    given-names: W. Taylor
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/willtfarrington/mimicwarehouse"
url: "https://github.com/willtfarrington/mimicwarehouse"
keywords:
  - MIMIC-IV
  - PhysioNet
  - electronic health records
  - DuckDB
  - Parquet
  - Polars
  - Streamlit
  - data warehouse
  - clinical data science
  - reproducible research
